          <div id="znid-162056828307"
            class="zn-element-wrapper 
                
              " 
            data-type="text"
            
          >
            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>Sweet, juicy, and streaked with red swirls, Lucky Cross is the golden child of Craig’s garden. </p><p><br></p><p>“The bees made the [Golden Cross], and it took me eight years to work on,” he said. “It’s the only tomato of that color that’s absolutely delicious.”</p><p><br></p><p>This sandwich skips the swine (because why not spare some <a href="https://www.aspca.org/protecting-farm-animals/animals-factory-farms#:~:text=The%20U.S.%20raises%20around%20120,farrowing%20crates%20to%20give%20birth">animal suffering</a> when we can) but still brings the sizzle. To start, toast two slices of hearty multigrain bread, then pile on thick slabs of Lucky Cross tomatoes, crunchy butter lettuce, and smoky plant-based bacon. We like <a href="https://myforestfoods.com/mybacon">MyBacon</a>, which crisps like the real deal and tastes remarkably similar. A swipe of roasted garlic mayo adds creaminess, while pickled shallots cut through the richness.&nbsp;</p></div>
            </div>
            
            
          </div>
        

